				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/tsar-erwin" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1970816); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1970816&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607958874" alt="Tsar Erwin" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1970816)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/tsar-erwin" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1970816); return false;" >Tsar Erwin</a></span> <span class="odate time_1454690246 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">05 Feb 2016 16:37</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2452176">
									

<p>So, I had read SCP-029 before and what I had gotten from it was that it was very dangerous but not unkillable, so I had thought of ways to kill her, various methods being pumping botulinum (Basically a nerve killing gas that results in a painful death after the nervous system fails.<br />
Or maybe even just a regular firing squad for the most part, but armed with experimental weapons that would theoretically kill her.<br />
Even thought about just putting warheads to foreheads, which would probably solve the Foundations problem if they really need to neutralize 029. But you just had a doctor have some unknown personnel put explosive rounds through her head and solve the entire problem.</p>
<p>Bravo!<br />
+1<br />
Also, I'd like to point out that this tale, through short in nature kinda did it for me. It was a quick read that even a newbie (Which I'm certainly not *coughcough*) could contextualize what was going on even if they didn't understand what exactly 029 is. Again, bravo and very good!</p>

